        "id": 1000835
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-01-13T09:59:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It feels weird to have a useBuiltInDnsResolver method on the AOSP API surface, because Android has a DNS resolver. Can we remove this? If we do remove it, do the other booleans in this builder continue to work?\n\nOTOH if we remove it, any CronetProvider that is based on this AOSP API will not support this method. That could prevent an app from using that CronetProvider.\n\nOne idea might be to set this @SystemApi so that the CronetProvider can use reflection perhaps? Maybe that can wait until a future CL.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 31,
        "startChar": 54,
        "endLine": 31,
        "endChar": 75
      },
      "revId": "c4a44cb03ea2e3611a1b1c34385892bf0eec66f7",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
