      "writtenOn": "2023-01-13T09:59:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The presence of this request object suggests that the intended usage (or one of the intended usages) of this API is to have one callback object that can be used for multiple requests.\n\nBut for that to be useful, calling equals() on the request passed in to this method and the original request built by the builder (and available to the app) should return true. If not, then that\u0027s really confusing.\n\nIf the expected usage is that there will always be one callback for each request, then why not make it the app\u0027s responsibility to keep track of what request corresponds to what callback, and remve this UrlRequest argument altogether?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 156,
        "startChar": 34,
        "endLine": 156,
        "endChar": 61
      },
